From: imykhailov <imykhailov@anaconda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Don't install the tests/ directory as package data

meson.build installs tests/__init__.py and tests/test_ewah_bool_utils.py
as a `tests` subpackage alongside the built extension modules, shipping
test files inside the installed conda package. Drop that install_sources
call; source_files in meta.yaml already makes the tests available for
the recipe's own test run.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -68,12 +68,6 @@ py.install_sources(
     subdir: 'ewah_bool_utils',
 )
 
-py.install_sources(
-    'tests/__init__.py',
-    'tests/test_ewah_bool_utils.py',
-    subdir: 'tests',
-)
-
 # include headers as easily locatable data files
 # to allow yt to link from a wheel
 install_data(
